  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating the pH, given the hydrogen ion concentration</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
The pH of an aqueous solution is related to its hydrogen ion concentration by the formula
\(
\mathrm{pH}=-\log_{10}([H^+]),
\)
where \([H^+]\) is the hydrogen ion concentration measured in moles per litre
(\(\mathrm{mol\,L^{-1}}\)).
</p>

<p>
<strong>(a)</strong> A laboratory technician measures a solution with a pH of
\( {@pH1@} \).
</p>

<p>
Use the formula to calculate the hydrogen ion concentration \([H^+]\) of this solution.
Give your answer in scientific notation to three significant figures.
</p>

<p>
\([H^+]=\) [[input:ans1]] \(\mathrm{mol\,L^{-1}}\)
[[validation:ans1]]
</p>

<hr />

<p>
<strong>(b)</strong> A second solution has a hydrogen ion concentration of
\( {@a@}\times10^{-{n}}\,\mathrm{mol\,L^{-1}} \).
</p>

<p>
Calculate the pH of this second solution, giving your answer to two decimal places.
</p>

<p>
\(\mathrm{pH}=\) [[input:ans2]]
[[validation:ans2]]
</p>

<hr />

<p>
<strong>(c)</strong> A solution has a hydrogen ion concentration of
\(10^{-{@p@}}\,\mathrm{mol\,L^{-1}}\).
</p>

<p>
Determine its pH.
</p>

<p>
\(\mathrm{pH}=\) [[input:ans3]]
[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt1]]
</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
